# tls-internal.caddy -- imported inside the site blocks when TLS_MODE=internal
# (what `make init` selects for dev domains: *.localtest.me, localhost, ...).
#
# Caddy mints its own CA ("Caddy Local Authority") in /data/caddy/pki and
# issues 12-hour leaf certificates for DOMAIN (and kuma.DOMAIN) from it,
# renewing them automatically. Because the caddy service runs as uid 1000,
# the CA files are owned by uid 1000 and n8n (also uid 1000) can read
# root.crt straight from the shared caddy_data volume -- that is how
# compose.dev.yml hands it to n8n via NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS. Browsers trust it
# after `make trust-ca`.
tls internal
